<title>NETHERLANDS: NEDLLOYD LOOKS TO BRING ECT INTO MERGER.</title>
<headline>NEDLLOYD LOOKS TO BRING ECT INTO MERGER.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Nedlloyd NV said on Wednesday it had supplied Europe Combined Terminals, in which it has a stake, of details on its possible inclusion in the newly formed container merger with Britain's P&amp;O .</p>
<p>Container group ECT is jointly owned by Nedlloyd, Pakhoed and Internatio Mueller, each with 30.56 percent and Dutch Railways with an 8.3 percent holding.</p>
<p>Nedlloyd said its share in ECT was to be brought into the newly merged group but in the event of a tranference, the other parties would have right to issue a bid within two months.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam newsroom  +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
